        "name": "Blob Schedule Configuration (EIP-7892)",
        "description": "Defines the BLOB_SCHEDULE configuration table that governs the maximum number of blobs permitted per block at any given epoch. This is a new mechanism in Fulu (via EIP-7892) that enables 'Blob Parameter Only Hardforks', allowing the blob limit to be adjusted via a schedule without requiring a full consensus-layer hard fork.",
